Why Are STATCOM Systems Becoming Important for European Power Grids?

Static Synchronous Compensators are power-electronic devices designed to provide dynamic reactive-power compensation within electricity networks.

They help regulate voltage by injecting or absorbing reactive power according to changing grid conditions. This capability is particularly important in electricity networks experiencing fluctuating loads and increasing renewable-energy generation.

Unlike conventional compensation equipment with slower response characteristics, STATCOM systems can provide rapid voltage-support functions through power-electronic converter technology.

Their application is becoming increasingly relevant as European utilities modernize transmission and distribution infrastructure.

